#X text 240 83 On an incoming list (l⁰ l¹ ...) outputs to the corresponding
outlet a message of the form [s⁰ l⁰( \, [s¹ l¹( \, etc. \, where s⁰
\, s¹ \, ... are the selectors given at object creation. The first
list element is paired with the first selector \, the second element
with the second selector \, and so on.;
#X text 240 184 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 209 • Turning a plain list into a set of property messages
— for example \, converting [1 2 3( into [@a 1( \, [@b 2( \, [@c 3(
for an object that expects named properties.;
